problem:
Let $S=\{1,2,3, \cdots, 15\}$, and take $n$ subsets $A_{1}, A_{2}, \cdots, A_{n}$ from $S$ satisfying the following conditions:
(1) $\left|A_{i}\right|=7, i=1,2, \cdots, n$;
(2) $\left|A_{i} \cap A_{j}\right| \leqslant 3(1 \leqslant i<j \leqslant n)$;
(3) For any three-element subset $M$ of $S$, there exists some $A_{k}$ such that $M \subset A_{k}$.
Find the minimum value of the number of such subsets $n$.
(1999 China National Team Selection Examination Problem)
